doc.details:
Creates and registers a new keyboard shortcut that can be triggered system-wide, regardless of which application has focus. The shortcut will trigger the provided callback when activated.

**Example**

```cpp
auto shortcut = manager.Register("Ctrl+Shift+Q", []() {
    std::cout << "Quick action triggered!" << std::endl;
});

if (!shortcut) {
    std::cerr << "Failed to register shortcut" << std::endl;
}
```

