doc.details:
Creates and registers a keyboard shortcut with additional configuration options such as scope (global vs application-local) and description.

**Example**

```cpp
ShortcutOptions options;
options.accelerator = "Ctrl+Alt+T";
options.callback = []() { OpenTerminal(); };
options.description = "Open terminal";
options.scope = ShortcutScope::Global;

auto shortcut = manager.Register(options);
```

Removes a previously registered shortcut from the system and stops monitoring for its activation.

**Example**

```cpp
ShortcutId id = shortcut->GetId();
bool success = manager.Unregister(id);
```

Removes all currently registered shortcuts from the system. This is useful for cleanup or when switching shortcut profiles.

**Example**

```cpp
int count = manager.UnregisterAll();
std::cout << "Unregistered " << count << " shortcuts" << std::endl;
```

Retrieves a previously registered shortcut using its assigned ID.

**Example**

```cpp
auto shortcut = manager.Get(shortcut_id);
if (shortcut) {
    std::cout << "Found shortcut: " << shortcut->GetAccelerator() << std::endl;
}
```

Retrieves a previously registered shortcut using its accelerator string.

**Example**

```cpp
auto shortcut = manager.Get("Ctrl+Shift+Q");
if (shortcut) {
    shortcut->SetEnabled(false);
}
```

Returns a vector containing all currently registered shortcut instances. The returned vector is a snapshot of the current state and modifications to it won't affect the internal shortcut registry.

**Example**

```cpp
auto all_shortcuts = manager.GetAll();
for (auto& shortcut : all_shortcuts) {
    std::cout << shortcut->GetAccelerator() << std::endl;
}
```

Returns shortcuts that match the specified scope (global or application-local).

**Example**

```cpp
auto global_shortcuts = manager.GetByScope(ShortcutScope::Global);
auto app_shortcuts = manager.GetByScope(ShortcutScope::Application);
```

Determines whether a keyboard shortcut string is available for use, i.e., not already registered by this application or conflicting with system shortcuts.

**Example**

```cpp
if (manager.IsAvailable("Ctrl+Shift+N")) {
    auto shortcut = manager.Register("Ctrl+Shift+N", callback);
} else {
    std::cout << "Shortcut already in use" << std::endl;
}
```

Checks if the provided accelerator string follows the correct format and contains valid key combinations. This is useful for validating user input before attempting registration.

**Example**

```cpp
if (manager.IsValidAccelerator("Ctrl+Shift+Q")) {
    // Valid format, safe to register
} else {
    std::cout << "Invalid shortcut format" << std::endl;
}
```

Allows temporarily disabling all shortcut processing without unregistering shortcuts. When disabled, shortcuts will remain registered but won't trigger their callbacks. This is useful for modal dialogs or when the application needs to temporarily suppress shortcut handling.

**Example**

```cpp
// Disable shortcuts during modal dialog
manager.SetEnabled(false);
ShowModalDialog();
manager.SetEnabled(true);  // Re-enable after dialog closes
```
